and how much of a problem is burnout. People are often unwilling to answer that, you know, truly, you know, honestly in that if they think there's going to be a downside on that, like that tap on the shoulder saying, what's wrong with you? there see a therapist. Because it is that kind of stigma and there could be negative consequences of it. So taking a focus not on do we have to have people self-identifies burned out before we do anything to improve the workplace?

