and how do we make changes there as well as helping people to relax and cope and, you know, and all that kind of thing. But a lot of those chronic job stressors that people are responding to or trying to deal with are ones over which they have no control and can't be changed or, you know, it shakes how they're able to live their life and do their day or, you know, night hours or whatever ship they're working. And so there's always a bigger, better approach to this. And it's not just by individual jobs. It's also about how do we make assignments, how do we decide how to get X done as opposed to

