and some are experimenting with a four-day work week. are these good ideas, do they effectively combat burnout, or is there something kind of counterintuitive about trying to solve burnout by telling people to get away from the workplace? You hit it right on the head. I mean, it's a strange thing, but often, you know, the best way to cope with, you know, work stress is not to work. And that makes the question, what's wrong with the work that, you know, to deal with it, you have to cut out, get away, take time off, take a vacation, you know, do fewer hours,

